(not loops) edges that are not adjacent — graph has four vertexes with odd degree, so Euler path doesn't exist. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Regular edges that are adjacent — graph has exactly two vertexes with odd degree, so Euler path exists. So, any pair of adjacent regular edges satisfies Igor. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" One of the edges is a loop — graph hasn't any vertex with the odd degree(if another chosen edge is a loop too) or has two of them(if another chosen edge is regular). So, any pair in which at least one edge is a loop satisfies Igor. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"So, we have to calculate the number of pairs of adjacent regular edges and add the answer for loops. For every vertex "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" we can calculate "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cnt"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the number of regular edges incoming in it. General number of adjacent regular edges is "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/a84dc7389724726e2b8b615703bca6cf32f31161e3749a54cf285b8d12c773b1.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". Also, we need to add the number of pairs with loops. Let's count "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"loop"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" — general number of loops in the graph. So we can add "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"loop"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"·("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1) to the answer. Now, we included pairs with two loops twice. That's why we need to subtract "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"loop"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the number of pairs with two loops. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Also, we need to check the graph to be connected by edges. If the graph is not connected then the answer is 0. We can do it using algorithms of DFS or BFS."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Complexity of the given solution if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"N"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"M"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"788C"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/788/problem/C"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"788C - The Great Mixing"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/09feda6bde054b3c27c79ba71ad2df7e8c8392ede52497ed7a67e5645baa5cc1.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" — needed concentration and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", ..., "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" — concentration of types we'll use."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/505f52f478f1640c59e62960ba5634895cf8332a50887b606c278208292a472e.png"},"kind":"image"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editor